  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative attributes the direct cause to degraded mounting bolt and/or degraded bushings, with further root-cause analysis still pending at time of report. HPCI was analyzed as remaining operable via engineering analysis despite Division II EECW/UHS being affected — modeled as INVOLVES (system affected/analyzed) rather than BACKED_UP_BY-only backup since narrative frames HPCI itself as the system whose operability was in question, but also states it 'remained operable' per analysis, so included as backup to the MDCT/UHS inoperability consequence. Division I UHS/MDCT fans (A, B, C) were operable throughout and are design/backup context per narrative ('Division I MDCT fans were operable... operable throughout this event') but not modeled as separate System nodes since they are the same UHS system, Division I. No previous similar occurrences were stated in the narrative, so no SIMILAR_TO stub LER emitted."
